  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 103 PM CDT Fri Aug 21 2026\n\nSummer heat continues through much of the next seven days, with \nSunday and Monday currently expected to be the hottest days of the \nforecast period. Highs will easily surpass 105 off the Caprock both \ndays, and may even exceed extreme heat criteria of 110 as well. \nCurrent NBM probs indicate about a 40-70% chance of exceeding 110 \ndegrees mainly in the lower elevations near and just west of \nChildress on both Sunday and Monday afternoons. Most areas on the \nCaprock will likely top out near or just above 105, which is \nstill nearing record highs this time of year. Storm chances will \nfall back below 10 percent during this time as well given \nunfavorable positioning of the ridge directly overhead. Model \nconsensus then indicates that the ridge will flatten and shift \nback westward toward the middle of the week which will bring a \nvery modest decrease in temperatures, although highs will remain \nabove normal. Depending on the exact position of the ridge, storm \nchances may also increase by Wednesday or Thursday as modest \nnorthwest flow aloft reestablishes over the region, but potential \nfor widespread rainfall still appears very low at this time.",
